#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""hertz-ctl: backend for the Hertz Radio Omarchy bar plugin.

`hertz-ctl daemon` runs for as long as the panel exists. It reads one-line
commands on stdin and streams JSON lines on stdout, so the QML side never
touches HTTP, files or the audio player itself:

  in   search {"genre": "Jazz", "country": "DE", "text": "", "page": 0}
       countries
       play <uuid> | toggle | stop | next | prev | retry
       volume <0-100> | mute | fav <uuid> | favorites
  out  {"type": "state", ...}      player snapshot (station, title, volume, ...)
       {"type": "stations", ...}   one page of directory results
       {"type": "favorites", ...}  saved stations
       {"type": "art", ...}        cached, local artwork path for a station
       {"type": "genres", ...}     genre names for the chip strip
       {"type": "countries", ...}  countries with station counts
       {"type": "error", ...}      something the user should see

Stations come from Radio Browser (https://www.radio-browser.info) through a
discovered mirror with failover. Playback runs in mpv over its JSON IPC
socket; mpv-mpris (part of Omarchy) publishes it to MPRIS, so media keys and
the omarchy.media widget work too. mpv is started in its own session, so the
stream survives a shell restart and the next daemon simply reattaches.

Other entry points, handy for testing: `hertz-ctl search <text>`,
`hertz-ctl genre <name>`, `hertz-ctl countries`, `hertz-ctl stop`.
"""

